#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    for (int row=1; row<=7; row++) {
        for (int col=1; col<=row-1; col++) {
            cout << " ";
        }
        for (int col=1; col<=2*(7-row)+1; col++) {
            cout << "*";
        }
        cout << endl;
    }
}



/<How the Code Works/>

Outer Loop (row from 1 to 7): Controls the total number of rows/lines in the pyramid,
executing exactly 7 times. First Inner Loop (col from 1 to row - 1): Responsible for printing
the leading spaces on each line. The number of spaces increases by 1 with each consecutive
row (starting with 0 spaces on the first line). Second Inner Loop (col from 1 to 2 * (7 - row) +
1): Responsible for printing the asterisks. The formula ensures the number of stars decreases
by 2 for each subsequent row, starting from 13 down to 1.
